§ `Regulation 2: Compoundable offence`

-- src:5 | 2. The offence under section 47 of the Act may be compounded by the Authority in accordance with section 57 (1) of the Act.
@ref reg 2 (src:5)
-- The only offence the Regulations prescribe as compoundable is the offence under s 47; s 57(1) caps the sum at $1,000.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the section number of the offence under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the offence may be compounded by the Authority in accordance with section 57(1), on` MEANS
    IF `the Composition of Offences Regulations as deposited are the text in force on` d THEN JUST (`the section number of the offence under the Act` EQUALS 47) ELSE NOTHING
